From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:34:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Developer role, Wi-Fi-first setup, Tailscale without sudo

- bootstrap.sh: requires an internet connection before starting and helps
  join Wi-Fi (nmtui); employee is a developer by default (sudo with own
  password, prompted at most hourly), --standard for no admin rights;
  Tailscale operator is waited for and verified, failing the step instead
  of warning; saved Wi-Fi networks are shared with all users.
- autoinstall.yaml: keeps the Wi-Fi joined in the installer for the first
  boot; ki-setup waits for a network before fetching, asks the role.
- New sbin/ki-user: set role and Tailscale operator on existing laptops.
- ki-check: admin rights checked against the recorded role; FAIL if the
  primary user is not the Tailscale operator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JnBUPn1w4G9w1HxKye31uj
